te-baseline-contamination, self-hosted-knowledge-read-set-collision, and toolchain-policy-architecture-index-gap; bind native evidence and identity; restrict classifications to anchor_candidate, challenge_candidate, or non_baseline_exploratory_candidate; and prevent seed promotion to a baseline or evaluation-set member.","reason":"The proposed set contains no permitted-domain obligation that represents these named-seed identities, classification vocabulary, and anti-promotion behavior independently.","source_ref":"execution-plans/2026-08-05-toolchain-core-skill-replay-portability-and-evaluation-seed/repair/round-7/recompilation-4/cer-repair-1/compiler-requirements.md#FR-6","subject":"Retained evaluation seeds"},{"behavior":"Require Stable provenance for source-supported existing behavior and require Candidate to contain the real change under evaluation.","reason":"The proposed obligations require immutable Stable and Candidate executions, but do not represent Stable eligibility provenance or the Candidate real-change requirement.","source_ref":"execution-plans/2026-08-05-toolchain-core-skill-replay-portability-and-evaluation-seed/repair/round-7/recompilation-4/cer-repair-1/compiler-requirements.md#FR-7","subject":"Stable and Candidate eligibility"},{"behavior":"Invalidate the aggregate for an expectation-forged Matrix Case.","reason":"Missing, copied, mislabeled, stale, reused, wrong-target, infrastructure-failed, and non-executed evidence are represented, but expectation-forged evidence is independently required by the retained Matrix contract and is absent.","source_ref":"execution-plans/2026-08-05-toolchain-core-skill-replay-portability-and-evaluation-seed/repair/round-7/recompilation-4/cer-repair-1/compiler-requirements.md#FR-8","subject":"Matrix aggregate"},{"behavior":"Freeze a non-empty Consumer Manifest before review and bind each Consumer's actual interface, input, command, output, result, and dependencies.","reason":"Bidirectional reconciliation is represented, but manifest freezing and the per-Consumer invocation binding are separate observable requirements not covered by the proposed obligations.","source_ref":"execution-plans/2026-08-05-toolchain-core-skill-replay-portability-and-evaluation-seed/repair/round-7/recompilation-4/cer-repair-1/compiler-requirements.md#FR-9","subject":"Consumer Manifest"},{"behavior":"During enable and re-enable, invoke the Candidate Route; during disable and rollback, invoke the Prior Route; reject configuration-only rollback; and require any non-applicability exception to be approved and bound before execution.","reason":"The proposed lifecycle obligations require real call surfaces and restoration, but do not independently preserve these route-direction, configuration-only, and pre-bound-exception behaviors.","source_ref":"execution-plans/2026-08-05-toolchain-core-skill-replay-portability-and-evaluation-seed/repair/round-7/recompilation-4/cer-repair-1/compiler-requirements.md#FR-10","subject":"Consumer route transitions"},{"behavior":"Require each behavioral obligation to have an independent fault witness and each non-behavioral obligation to have a deterministic violation witness.","reason":"The proposed Exact Cover obligations require links and zero orphans, but do not separately require the source-defined witness type for each obligation class.","source_ref":"execution-plans/2026-08-05-toolchain-core-skill-replay-portability-and-evaluation-seed/repair/round-7/recompilation-4/cer-repair-1/compiler-requirements.md#FR-11","subject":"Atomic Obligation witnesses"},{"behavior":"Bind the Current Snapshot to the Git baseline, Skill-input v2 selection and content, code, fixtures, contracts, Consumers, tests, targets, validators, dependencies, sources, evidence, and any versioned normalization policy.","reason":"A complete Current Snapshot is required generically, but the independently observable required binding members are not represented individually or as a complete enumerated set.","so